%% How the language model scores a room without ever holding the tick up
sequenceDiagram
  participant INT as Tick loop<br/>(every tick)
  participant DET as LLM detector
  participant RULE as Fusion rule
  participant WRK as Worker<br/>(background)
  participant EP as Language model<br/>(HTTPS)
  rect rgb(232, 240, 252)
    INT->>DET: 1: P(fire) for each room?
    Note over DET: 2: quiet room? nothing to ask
    Note over DET: 3: 10 s since last asked? queue the readings
    alt answer younger than 60 s
      DET-->>INT: 4a: the model's P(fire), at once
    else no answer, or too old
      DET->>RULE: 4b: ask the rule
      RULE-->>INT: the rule's P(fire)
    end
  end
  rect rgb(240, 232, 252)
    WRK->>WRK: 5: every 250 ms: take the queue,<br/>most suspicious room first
    WRK->>EP: 6: one room's readings, one question at a time
    EP-->>WRK: 7: about 8 s later: P(fire), evidence, reason
    Note over WRK: 8: check the reply. A bad one is thrown away
    WRK->>DET: 9: keep the answer, write it to the journal
  end
  Note over DET: 10: speed limit = 60 s / (2 x 8 s), about 3x
